cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "TwinLens: an interpretability digital twin for LLMs"
abstract: >-
  TwinLens builds a digital twin of a language model's internals from transcoders,
  predicts the effect of feature interventions, and verifies each prediction against
  the real model. It shows that attribution graphs predict interventions poorly
  because they drop two derivatives (LayerNorm scale and attention pattern), and that
  restoring them keeps the graph linear while matching the nonlinear replacement model.
